sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/wolfram2002-ch10-17> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "Although most nested patterns have no obvious relation to ordinary mathematical functions, a formula for the color of each cell of any nested pattern can probably be found in terms of suitably generalized hypergeometric functions or similar generalizations of traditional functions.";
    dc:type "mathematical";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Every nested pattern likely has a formula in generalized hypergeometric functions";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Stephen Wolfram, A New Kind of Science (Champaign, IL: Wolfram Media, 2002), Chapter 10, “Processes of Perception and Analysis”; section “Traditional Mathematics and Mathematical Formulas” (from p. 606), p. 612. Scope: nested patterns generated by substitution systems"
}
